# <%= it.ctx.name %>

A Node-RED custom node scaffolded with [flowup](https://github.com/wry-smile/flowup).

## UI Stack

<% if (it.ctx.clientFramework === 'vue') { %>- **Vue** (SFC, .vue files)
<% } else if (it.ctx.clientFramework === 'svelte') { %>- **Svelte** (.svelte files)
<% } else if (it.ctx.clientFramework === 'preact') { %>- **Preact** (TSX files)
<% } else if (it.ctx.clientFramework === 'solid') { %>- **Solid** (TSX files)
<% } else { %>- Plain HTML + TypeScript (no UI framework)
<% } %>
<% if (it.ctx.unocss) { %>- **UnoCSS Wind4** (scoped atomic CSS)
<% } %>

## Client Helpers

<% if (it.ctx.clientFramework !== 'vanilla' || it.ctx.unocss) { %>- `@wry-smile/flowup/client` provides shared editor helpers.
<% if (it.ctx.clientFramework !== 'vanilla') { %>- `@wry-smile/flowup/client/<%= it.ctx.clientFramework %>` provides the framework-specific hydrate adapter.
<% } %>
<% } %>
<% if (it.ctx.clientFramework === 'vue') { %>- Vue templates include `client/hydrate.ts`.
<% } %>
<% if (it.ctx.clientFramework === 'svelte') { %>- Svelte templates include `client/App.svelte` and `client/hydrate.ts`.
<% } %>
<% if (it.ctx.clientFramework === 'preact' || it.ctx.clientFramework === 'solid') { %>- <%= it.ctx.clientFramework %> templates include TSX components and editor mount logic.
<% } %>
<% if (it.ctx.unocss) { %>- UnoCSS styles are scoped to `data-flowup-scope`; popup mount nodes need the same attribute.
<% } %>
- Shared constants are generated in `constant/index.ts`.

## Layout

```
<%= it.ctx.name %>/
├── package.json
├── flowup.config.ts
├── constant/
├── runtime/
├── client/
├── types/
├── locales/
├── icons/
└── resources/
```

## Build

```
pnpm install
pnpm build
```

## Preview in Node-RED

```
pnpm dev
```

Flowup builds the package and starts Node-RED with `nodesDir` pointing at `dist/`. Source changes trigger a rebuild and one restart after the final successful build. Configure the preview with `nodeRed` in `flowup.config.ts`.

Produces `dist/<%= it.ctx.name %>.js`, `dist/<%= it.ctx.name %>.html`, locales, icons, resources, and `flowup.manifest.json`.

## Package

```
pnpm build
npm pack --dry-run
```

<% if (it.ctx.clientFramework === 'vanilla' && !it.ctx.unocss) { %>
## Optional: Vue / UnoCSS

This starter uses plain HTML and TypeScript by default. To add Vue or UnoCSS:

```bash
pnpm add -D @vitejs/plugin-vue unocss
```

Then import and add the plugins in `flowup.config.ts`:

```ts
import vue from '@vitejs/plugin-vue'
import UnoCSS from 'unocss/vite'
import { defineConfig, presetFlowupWind4 } from '@wry-smile/flowup'

const scope = '<%= it.ctx.name %>'
export default defineConfig({
  scope,
  client: { plugins: [UnoCSS({ presets: [presetFlowupWind4({ scope })] }), vue()] },
})
```
<% } %>
